From b5871e43fbb29ac5745f70e9c5678019c40f991a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:41:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not stand still for two reads on the way back from a won
 battle

The field's music font (a seek and 27 sectors) and the background's .TFS header (2 sectors from the start of the file, for
palettes that are already resident) were read before the world ran again; on the way back from a won fight the picture stood
still for both (1.0 s in PCSX-Redux, about 2 s on a device). The header is not read again when the same map is reopened (a
battle exit, the ring's own reopening, the jukebox), and with QUICK BATTLES on the field's font goes through the file queue
like the battle's. The ring opens at once and leaves the slots under the font alone until it is in; until then playMusic,
the next queued font and any synchronous read over its staging wait for it, so the music and the load area keep the
original's order. The ring's prefetch then waits for the BTL_REL read ahead to be queued (at most 90 vsyncs), and the read
ahead is not queued while a background tile is being read: queueing waits for that read, and the first tile after the font
seeks across the disc (0.7 s standing still).
